{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"16907fe07c4bb266d28d66d5996b9f9dfe9a0d925dbb68ba0e09c89b36b5cb0d","digest":{"component_or_area":"test infrastructure / conftest","key_entities":["_rebar_repo_template","tests/interfaces/conftest.py","rebar.list_tickets()","tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_template_stays_virgin",".rebar","MonkeyPatch.context()"],"problem_keywords":["fixture assertion","test isolation","template virgin state","ticket seeding"],"propositions":["The _rebar_repo_template fixture asserts template has no .rebar directory but was not asserting the template contains no tickets.","Ticket seeding invariant is checked only in test_template_stays_virgin which protects only when that specific test is selected, leaving narrowed runs like pytest tests/interfaces/store without protection.","The missing no-tickets assertion must run inside the MonkeyPatch context where REBAR_ROOT and cwd are pinned to the template, allowing rebar.list_tickets() to work correctly.","Pre-warming the template with tickets would silently invert emptiness assertions in session-log and lifecycle tests that rely on the template being virgin."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"ad49f17f-3ae1-46af-813d-cd2a5470d9b2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787876408714623507,"uuid":"f35c55eb-9770-4089-a76b-695aae40e5e0"}